    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The objective of these Case Studies is to record, in a consistent format, studies of woodframe buildings damaged in the Northridge Earthquake of 1994 to benefit the building community as well as the other Element of the CUREE-Caltech Woodrame Project, namely:\r\n\r\n• The Codes and Standards Element, to develop new design guidelines and Code provisions;\r\n• The Economic Aspects Element, to improve loss estimation for woodframe buildings;\r\n• The Education and Outreach Element, to develop education tools for various constituencies.\r\n\r\nTable of Contents:\r\n\r\nIntroduction\r\nSummary\r\nCase Study Contents\r\nCase Study Overview\r\nConclusions\r\nExcerpts from Case Study Findings\r\nBibliography\r\n\r\nCase Study 2 - Sherman Court Condominiums\r\n\r\nCase Study 3 - Century Park Place Phase 2\r\n\r\nCase Study 4 - Dickens Street Condominiums\r\n\r\nCase Study 5 - Northridge Garden Apartments\r\n\r\nCase Study 6 - Northridge Meadows Apartments\r\n\r\nCase Study 7 - Sherman Oaks Condominiums Building\r\n\r\nCase Study 8 - Santa Clarita Apartment Complex\r\n\r\nCase Study 9 - Northridge Complex\r\n\r\nCase Study 10 - Fulton (Building F)\r\n\r\nCase Study 11 - Hazeltine (Building H)\r\n\r\nCase Study 12 - Gallagher (Building G)\r\n\r\nCase Study 13 - Kleinman (Building K)\r\n\r\nCase Study 14 - Olsen (Building O)\r\n\r\nCase Study 15 - Raedeke (Building R)\r\n\r\nCase Study 16 - Smith (Building S)\r\n\r\nCase Study 17 - CSUN Satellite Student Union Center",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
